WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
from Gem State Chronicle published March 19th, 2026.

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.880
Rest in peace, Rick Hogeboom.

3
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.960
Last night, as I was finishing a meeting

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.619
of the Eagle Public Library Board of Trustees,

5
00:00:10.619 --> 00:00:13.680
I heard sirens and saw numerous emergency vehicles

6
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.899
rushing to Eagle City Hall.

7
00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:17.920
Mayors from across the region had gathered

8
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.600
for a meeting of the Treasure Valley Partnership,

9
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.040
and I wondered what had happened.

10
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.479
Nampa Mayor Rick Hogeboom was the last person

11
00:00:25.479 --> 00:00:27.680
I expected to have a medical emergency.

12
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.700
He was fairly young, only four years older than me,

13
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.080
healthy and full of energy and vitality.

14
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.520
I was shocked when I heard that he had collapsed

15
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.619
and deeply saddened to learn later that he had passed away.

16
00:00:41.639 --> 00:00:44.279
My own mayor, Brad Pike of Eagle,

17
00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:48.119
quickly administered CPR, but to no avail.

18
00:00:48.119 --> 00:00:50.240
It's a devastating loss for Nampa

19
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.380
and for Idaho as a whole.

20
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.560
When he announced his campaign for mayor,

21
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.400
I saw him as the surest bet in the state.

22
00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.639
He earned support from conservatives, moderates,

23
00:00:59.639 --> 00:01:01.560
and even liberals at the Idaho Statesman

24
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.559
because of his record of bold and competent leadership,

25
00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:06.760
of how cities and counties function,

26
00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.639
funding, growth, and quality of life.

27
00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:12.300
I appreciated his insight as I've learned more

28
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.680
about this side of politics.

29
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.739
I only had a handful of in-person conversations with Rick,

30
00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:20.519
but I found them extremely valuable.

31
00:01:20.519 --> 00:01:23.199
I had hoped to connect with him again after his election

32
00:01:23.199 --> 00:01:25.019
and swearing in as Nampa's mayor,

33
00:01:25.019 --> 00:01:27.279
but I assumed there was no hurry.

34
00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.519
I had hoped to meet him again,

35
00:01:29.519 --> 00:01:32.720
but I was afraid that we had all the time in the world.

36
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.919
It's a tragic reminder that life can be short,

37
00:01:35.919 --> 00:01:38.199
and none of us are guaranteed tomorrow.

38
00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.919
Rick first reached out to me a couple of years ago

39
00:01:41.919 --> 00:01:44.000
after reading some of my writing.

40
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.839
He was curious, not about political ideas,

41
00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:49.199
but about my Christian faith.

42
00:01:49.199 --> 00:01:51.319
His own faith was evident in every aspect

43
00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:52.559
of his life and work,

44
00:01:52.559 --> 00:01:55.620
and I know of few better witnesses for Jesus Christ

45
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.099
Rick was everything citizens want in a public servant

46
00:01:58.099 --> 00:01:59.099
and elected leader.

47
00:01:59.099 --> 00:02:01.260
He surely had a long career ahead of him,

48
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.819
but it was cut short far too soon.

49
00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:07.900
Rick Hogeboom was a husband, father, pastor, and leader.

50
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.860
His loss will be keenly felt across Idaho,

51
00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.059
especially in Nampa, which has lost a promising young mayor.

52
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.720
Above all, keep his wife and five children in your prayers

53
00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.279
as they face this sudden tragedy.

54
00:02:20.279 --> 00:02:21.779
I hope this tragedy reminds us

55
00:02:21.779 --> 00:02:23.860
to keep our priorities in order,

56
00:02:23.899 --> 00:02:25.380
to remember what truly matters

57
00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.419
in how we spend the limited time and energy

58
00:02:27.419 --> 00:02:28.820
we've been given.

59
00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.139
After all, none of us knows how long we have.

60
00:02:32.139 --> 00:02:35.300
May his memory be an example to other public servants

61
00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.820
and a blessing to us all.
